How to Fix Google Cloud ADC / Project ID Issues with agents-cli (Vertex AI / Gemini)
If you are running into HTTP 500: Internal Server Error or DefaultCredentialsError when running agents-cli locally, it is usually because the agent cannot find your Google Cloud credentials or project ID.

Here is the step-by-step guide to properly authenticate and configure your local environment:

Authenticate with Google Cloud (ADC)
First, log in to set up your Application Default Credentials (ADC) so local libraries can authenticate:

bash
gcloud auth application-default login
This will open your web browser to log in with your Google Cloud account.

Set your Google Cloud Project ID
Define your target Google Cloud Project ID in your terminal session. Replace your-gcp-project-id with your actual project ID from the GCP Console:

bash
export GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT="your-gcp-project-id"
Configure the Quota Project for your local credentials
To prevent quota limit or API enablement errors during execution, link your GCP project as the quota project for your ADC credentials:

bash
gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project your-gcp-project-id
Configure SDK settings (Optional / Agent Specific)
If your agent uses Vertex AI via the GenAI SDK, ensure the SDK is instructed to route requests through Vertex:

bash
export GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI="True"
Once these steps are completed, your local server will have all the necessary credentials and configuration to run successfully. You can verify and run your agent with:

bash
agents-cli run "Hello, how are you?"
